Subject: [PATCH] recovery and latency fixes on 2 x DGX Spark (both ranks)

On top of 0063 (the bundle-13 tree), bundle 14. A stream's first token goes out before its first drafter pass, which
otherwise ran inside every drafting reply's time to first token. A drafter pass that fails on a failed RDMA ring ends the
process with status 75, as a round and a prompt pass already did, instead of failing until the 300 s stall exit. The
server's writes never block: each send takes the room the socket has, and a client that stops reading is given up after
write_ms without progress (a blocking write past that room waited with no timeout). A peer that sent a byte and closed
is seen as gone (POLLRDHUP). Tokens are unchanged. CPU-tested with four red copies, source-reviewed twice, and A/B-checked
on the pair: 92/92 exact against 0063, TTFT by arrival rank -0.1 to -3.5 % in all but one cell (research/
LOCAL-STACK-20261106.md, "Bundle 14"). Generated with `git diff --binary` in a checkout of the 0063 tree; `git apply` of it
gives the served source file for file (1286 files, sha256-compared).

